-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party references and their licenses
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

k2kremote/midi_bridge.py
  Wraps the psobot/k2000 SysEx library as a runtime dependency (no source
  code copied):
    k2000 — Python library for the Kurzweil K2 series
    Copyright (C) 2022-2023  Peter Sobot
    https://github.com/psobot/k2000
    License: MIT
  The throttled-output queue, the MultiIn merged-input facade, and the split
  send/receive connection logic are ported from:
    mpc2emu (tests/re_banks/krz_sysex_live.py)
    Copyright (C) 2025-2026  mpc2emu contributors
    License: GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)
  The reverse-engineered MIDI behaviour these encode (the 120 ms SysEx flood
  floor, dynamic multi-port sub-port reassignment, broadcast device id) is
  documented in the mpc2emu project's docs/k2000r_midi_comms.md, verified on real
  K2000R hardware. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

k2kremote/braille.py
  Original work. Renders the 240x64 pixel array produced at runtime by
  psobot/k2000's ScreenReply.to_pixel_array (MIT, Peter Sobot).
  No third-party source code used. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

All other files (k2kremote/__init__.py, tests)
  Original work. Released under GPL-2.0-or-later.

